{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:StochasticMechanics.ClassicalLimitFunctor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"StochasticMechanics.ClassicalLimitFunctor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Functor","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.not_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.not_full","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The functor is NOT full: quantum information is lost in the limit.\nThere exist morphisms in C_1 not in the image of L. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.braiding_trivializes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.braiding_trivializes","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Quantum gap collapse: ℏ_q → 0 as q → 1.\nExpressed as: the functor sends the braiding to the symmetric swap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.functorMonoidal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.functorMonoidal","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The monoidal structure on `functor`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.functor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.functor","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The underlying functor, together with its monoidal structure.\n\nMathlib replaced the bundled `MonoidalFunctor Cq C1` with a plain\nfunctor carrying a `Functor.Monoidal` **typeclass**, so the bundle is\nsplit in two here. `functor.toFunctor` and `functor.μIso X Y` become\n`functor` and `Functor.Monoidal.μIso functor X Y` accordingly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ClassicalLimitFunctor","kind":"structure","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.lean#L25-L62","doc":"**Classical limit functor** `L : C_q → C_1`.\n\nSends the braided monoidal category `C_q` (at deformation parameter q)\nto the symmetric monoidal category `C_1` (at q = 1). The functor\ncollapses the quantum gap, smooths the q-differential, and trivializes\nthe braiding.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:classical-limit-functor}`\nRef: [leitner2026] Chapter 8, Section 5\n\n**`is_exact : Prop` removed 2026-09-07 — universe-`Prop` typed, neither read\nnor constructed. Exactness of the functor needs additive structure on `Cq`\nand `C1`, which this structure does not require.** ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:classical-limit-functor","label":"def:classical-limit-functor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/classical-limit-functor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}